title: Media
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: party_affairs
view-if: media_timer <= 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; media_timer += 6;
card-image: img/sangerbund.jpg

= Media

Between sympathetic outlets, independent media, and our own social media presence, the coalition has real reach. How should we use it?

- @commercial
- @campaign
- @ideological
- @digital
- @digital_2
- @digital_3
- @digital_4
- @return: We should not do anything with media at the moment.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@commercial
title: Broaden the appeal of our media beyond committed supporters.
subtitle: This might upset ideological purists, but it may bring in more funds and reach beyond our existing base.
on-arrival: resources += 1; commercialized_media += 1; suburban_dem += 4*(1 - dissent); college_educated_dem += 3*(1-dissent); insurgent_dissent += 10; labor_left_dissent += 10

Our broader-appeal media brings in more funding. However, the insurgent and labor-left wings express real displeasure at the softened messaging.

@campaign
title: The purpose of our media is to win elections.
subtitle: Our media will focus squarely on the electoral campaign.
on-arrival: campaign_media += 1; working_class_dem += 4*(1 - dissent); black_voters_dem += 2*(1-dissent);

Our campaign media is mostly reaching people already receptive to us, but it must be doing *something*, or at least that's what we tell ourselves.

@ideological
title: We will have vibrant ideological debate across our media ecosystem.
subtitle: There will be space for every faction to air its views.
on-arrival: insurgent_dissent -= 6; labor_left_dissent -= 6; progressive_dissent -= 6; establishment_dem_dissent -= 6; blue_dog_dissent -= 6

This has been our media course so far, and it has mostly paved over the tensions within the coalition.

@digital
title: Invest seriously in our own digital media operation.
subtitle: -2 resources
choose-if: resources >= 2
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: digital_media = 0
on-arrival: digital_media += 1; resources -= 2; college_educated_dem += 4*(1 - dissent); suburban_dem += 3*(1 - dissent); working_class_dem += 2*(1 - dissent); labor_left_dissent += 5; socialism += 3*(1 - dissent); polarization -= 3*(1 - dissent) if foreign_policy_restraint > 1; pro_democracy += 3*(1-dissent) if authoritarian_urgency > 1

Our new digital media operation - video, podcasts, and organized social media presence - lets us reach people in a more direct and personal way than earned press coverage ever did. It skews younger and more online, a fact our labor-left comrades are painfully aware of.

@digital_2
title: We should keep building out our digital media operation.
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: digital_media > 0 and digital_media <= 3
on-arrival: digital_media += 1; resources -= 1; college_educated_dem += 5*(1 - dissent); suburban_dem += 3*(1 - dissent); working_class_dem += 3*(1 - dissent); socialism += 3*(1 - dissent); polarization -= 3*(1 - dissent)*(foreign_policy_restraint-2) if foreign_policy_restraint > 2; pro_democracy += 3*(1-dissent)*(authoritarian_urgency-2) if authoritarian_urgency > 2

Our digital operation has a real mix of political content and genuine cultural reach, and it's working.

@digital_3
title: We should keep building out our digital media operation.
subtitle: It's now largely self-sustaining and doesn't require more resources.
view-if: digital_media > 3 and digital_media <= 5
on-arrival: digital_media += 1; college_educated_dem += 5*(1 - dissent); suburban_dem += 4*(1 - dissent); working_class_dem += 4*(1 - dissent); rural_dem += 3*(1 - dissent); latino_voters_dem += 2*(1-dissent); socialism += 3*(1 - dissent); polarization -= 3*(1 - dissent)*(foreign_policy_restraint-2) if foreign_policy_restraint > 2; pro_democracy += 3*(1-dissent)*(authoritarian_urgency-2) if authoritarian_urgency > 2

Our media operation has become a genuinely effective tool for spreading our message.

@digital_4
title: We should keep supporting our digital operation.
subtitle: As the online landscape gets more crowded, the novelty is wearing off. -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: digital_media > 3 and digital_media >= 6 and digital_media <= 9
on-arrival: digital_media += 1; resources -= 1; college_educated_dem += 3*(1 - dissent); suburban_dem += 2*(1 - dissent); working_class_dem += 3*(1 - dissent); rural_dem += 2*(1 - dissent); latino_voters_dem += 2*(1-dissent); socialism += 2*(1 - dissent); polarization -= 2*(1 - dissent)*(foreign_policy_restraint-2) if foreign_policy_restraint > 2; pro_democracy += 2*(1-dissent)*(authoritarian_urgency-2) if authoritarian_urgency > 2

We keep investing, but the online landscape is more saturated and more contested than ever, making it harder to break through the noise.
